@Ferroin what's your `queue/hw_sector_size` ? Mine happens to be `512`, maybe that's why we haven't spotted this bug.

@intelfx might be right, considering we calculate unallocated as:
```
disk_unallocated = node->all_disks_total - disk_total;
```
where 
```
node->all_disks_total += d->size * d->hw_sector_size;
```

Now, `d->hw_sector_size` is read from `queue/hw_sector_size`, but we should probably change that to a fixed value of 512, as [Linux always considers sectors to be 512 bytes long, independently of the devices real block size](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/include/linux/types.h#L120-L121), so I guess `d->size` is always measured in `512-byte` sectors as well.
